  "q": "2.46 g of hydrated magnesium sulfate, \\(\\text{MgSO}_4 \\cdot x\\text{H}_2\\text{O}\\), is heated to constant mass, leaving 1.20 g of anhydrous \\(\\text{MgSO}_4\\). What is \\(x\\)? (\\(M_r\\): \\(\\text{MgSO}_4 = 120\\), \\(\\text{H}_2\\text{O} = 18\\))",
